WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.534 line:92%
-So lovely to have you here.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.936 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-So lovely to be here.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:03.870 line:92%
-So, this is very exciting.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.573
You will be starting January 3rd
in Congress.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:10.076
You, however,
also very impressive in 2016 --

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
Teacher of the Year --
and you met President Obama.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-And you...

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:18.284 size:84% position:42%
-Oh, yeah. [ Laughs ]
-This is -- I'm glad --

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I do want to --
We brought a clip.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- two years later,
it seems like

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
you still are processing
that you met President Obama.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's just show everyone
how you reacted then.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.571 line:92%
-It is now my privilege...

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.673 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.877 line:92%
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sorry.
Don't kick me out.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No, you're doing good.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jahana cares
about the example she sets

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
as much as the exams
that she scores.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
What...

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.090 line:92%
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Oh, you --

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
you just need to settle down.
-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:06.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you have to tell me...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-Did...

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.904 line:92%
When you left there in 2016,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you already have
in your head

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.339 line:92%
that you wanted to come back,

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you wanted
to run for office?

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.377
-I had in my head, "They're
never letting me back in here."

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So what steps led
to you deciding to --

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.383 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to make a run for this?

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, 2016
was a really tricky year.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm. Yep.
-A lot happened.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:33.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm
a high-school history teacher.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.961 line:92%
I had really been teaching kids

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get involved
in their communities,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.099 line:92%
to be a part of the solution.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:42.502
And it felt like that narrative
was slipping away,

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people
weren't conducting themselves

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.475
in a way
that was solution driven, so...

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So now you're in D.C.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.312
-And it is freshman orientation.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.981
-And there are a lot of freshmen
there this year,

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:58.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of new congresspeople
in D.C.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:02.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
As a teacher, does it feel
like actual orientation

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you would have
for students?

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely not.
-Okay.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:06.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely not.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all,
children conduct themselves

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
so much more responsibly
than adults.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
-Yeah.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.307 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Young people are open

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:26.146
to just hearing about ideas
that are different from theirs,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.714 line:92%
learning about other people.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:30.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, of course,
you have an adult in the room

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:35.421
who says, you know, these are
parameters by which we behave.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
All bets are off in D.C.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.926
-It's a lot different.
Orientation was a lot different.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.862 line:92%
-I also -- you know, anyone --

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
when Republicans
come in to serve,

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:45.832 line:92%
when Democrats come in to serve,

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you are
freshmen congresspeople,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of people have run
on the idea

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.271 line:92%
that Congress is dysfunctional.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.706
This is, I would say,
the one thing that's nonpartisan

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.276
is everybody says what's
currently there is a mess.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.111
Have you found it dysfunctional
already?

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.781
-Well, I mean, I don't want
to criticize anyone because,

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:05.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
of course, they have a system
by which they operate.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.053 line:92%
But, I mean, you go in --

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:11.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
everything is separated
by Republican and Democrat.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.058 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Even our first vote --

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
literally, it took us
about two hours to vote.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
You picked up a paper
on one side of the room.

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:18.798 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You checked a box.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:19.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
You took it
to the other side of the room.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.869
And I'm sitting there like, "You
know, there's an app for that."

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like...
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
We could have done this
in five minutes.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:27.207 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm just watching it,
because you hear.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like
"Oh, my God, this is real."

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:31.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So is it --
-It's a good thing we're here.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a good thing we're here.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:35.882 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
it just seems like so --

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.652
I mean -- So, there are just
so many inefficiencies, right?

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not even about politics.
-Right.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.856
-Just people doing things
in a slow, stupid way.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-What he said.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I said it. I said it.
-Yes.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.562 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I think --
and a lot of it is just,

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is how
we've always done it.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:55.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And in my mind, I'm thinking,
but is it a rule?

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can we change it?
-Yeah.

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.107 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Can we do it different?

